<title>USA: Japan tops export market list for NY airports.</title>
<headline>Japan tops export market list for NY airports.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan was the leading gateway for cargo exports from John F. Kennedy airport and Newark airport in the period January to September 1996. The Port Authority of New York and New Jersey said.</p>
<p>The top ten markets by country for exports in tonnes for the first nine months of 1996 were</p>
<p> 1  Japan		     44,564</p>
<p> 2  United Kingdom	  37,791</p>
<p> 3  Germany		   27,164</p>
<p> 4  Korea		     18,806</p>
<p> 5  Israel		    16,876</p>
<p> 6  France		    15,155</p>
<p> 7  Singapore		 13,825</p>
<p> 8  Italy		     13,208</p>
<p> 9  Netherlands	     12,869</p>
<p> 10 Brazil		    10,501</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax:5017</p>
</text>
